\begin_layout Subsection
Manage Command 
\end_layout

\begin_layout Standard
The web client interacts with a PDV instance by use of the manage command.
 Below are the commands that the web client issues to a particular PDV instance.
 All the commands have a prefix: /<PDV>/manage.
 All data passed between the web client and the PDV instance is encrypted
 with the symmetric key established in the log on procedure.
\end_layout

\begin_layout Itemize
Adding apps, data streams, receivers:
\end_layout

\begin_deeper
\begin_layout Itemize
/add/apps/<app_name>
\end_layout

\begin_layout Itemize
/add/datastreams/<app_name>/<datastream_name> 
\end_layout

\begin_layout Itemize
/add/receiver/<app_name>/<datastream_name>/<receiver_uri>
\end_layout

\end_deeper
\begin_layout Itemize
Retrieving a data record:
\end_layout

\begin_deeper
\begin_layout Itemize
/getcontent/<app_name>/<ds_name>/<data_id>
\end_layout

\end_deeper
\begin_layout Itemize
Retrieving a list of available apps, datastreams, and data records:
\end_layout

\begin_deeper
\begin_layout Itemize
/list/apps 
\end_layout

\begin_layout Itemize
/list/datastreams/<app_name> 
\end_layout

\begin_layout Itemize
/list/datarecords/<app_name>/<datastream_name>
\end_layout

\end_deeper
\begin_layout Itemize
Setting the publisher for a data stream:
\end_layout

\begin_deeper
\begin_layout Itemize
/set_publisher/<app_name>/<datastream_name>/<publisher_uri>
\end_layout

\end_deeper
\begin_layout Section
Known Issues and Future Work
\end_layout

\begin_layout Standard
One issue with modifying a PDV instance (e.g.
 adding an app, data stream, or receiver) is that the changes are not immediatel
y reflected by the web client as a result of the NDN cache.
 For example, if we add an app then ask to re-list the apps, the old, cached
 list of apps is returned to the web client, rather than the updated list
 with the new app.
\end_layout

\begin_layout Standard
In order for the initial key exchange to work correctly, it seems as though
 everything must be freshly restarted.
 That is, if either the PDC or web client are restarted, the logon procedure
 and setup of a symmetric key fails.
 As such, ccnd, mongodb, the pdc, and the web client must be freshly started
 in order for the logon procedure to work correctly.
\end_layout

\begin_layout Standard
As of now, interests between the web client and PDC are not yet signed.
 In order to augment security, interests should be signed using the symmetric
 key.
 Furthermore, objects transmitted between the two entities should be done
 via protobufs, as implementations of iBSONExportable do not seem to work
 reliably.
 This includes, but is not limited to, the user's logon credentials and
 the web client's public key.
 The ability to remove apps and datastreams should also be implemented.
\end_layout

